# Cloudflare Pages headers. Committed, no build.
#
# EVERYTHING REVALIDATES, NOTHING SITS AT THE EDGE. Measured 2026-09-21: a deploy that changed one
# module reported success, curl fetched the new bytes, and every browser at the MCI edge kept getting
# the OLD module for a further twelve minutes and counting -- because a module import is a CORS
# request with an Origin header, Cloudflare keys that variant separately, and the deploy's purge did
# not reach it. This site is a few hundred small files whose whole point is that what was deployed is
# what you get, so the edge is told not to keep any of it and browsers are told to ask every time
# (an ETag round-trip, 304 if unchanged). bin/deploy's post-check fetches the CORS variant of every
# file and refuses to finish while any one of them differs from the tree.
#
# MEASURED AFTER THIS LANDED: the Pages origin (you-discoverywritten.pages.dev) serves max-age=0 as
# asked; the custom domain rewrites it to max-age=300 and caches anyway. That is a ZONE setting on
# discoverywritten.com (Caching → Configuration: Browser Cache TTL / a Cache Rule), which overrides
# what the origin says, and only the dashboard can change it: a Cache Rule for this hostname set to
# Bypass, plus one Purge to clear what is already held. This file stays true for the origin.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
